# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — CLAUDE.md §1.5.
# Every new setting added to the code gets a line here, or the next person
# cannot start the project.

NODE_ENV=development

# --- API ---------------------------------------------------------------
PORT=3001
# Comma-separated exact origins. Never "*", never a wildcard pattern.
# Production: https://nomadkids.mn
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# --- Database ----------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://kinder:kinder@localhost:5434/kinder

# ⚠ The integration suite TRUNCATEs every table between test cases. Point it at
# its own database or `pnpm test` empties the one above — including whatever
# `seed:demo` just put there, silently, every single run.
#
# Create it once:
#   pnpm --filter @kinder/api test:db:setup
#
# Optional. CI leaves it unset because its DATABASE_URL is already a throwaway
# service container; `test/setup.ts` warns when that is the case.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://kinder:kinder@localhost:5434/kinder_test

# Only needed to GENERATE a migration (`prisma migrate diff`), never to apply
# one. ⚠ Prisma drops and recreates this database on every use — never point it
# at anything you care about.
SHADOW_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://kinder:kinder@localhost:5434/kinder_shadow

# --- Redis (BullMQ) ----------------------------------------------------
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6380

# Whether THIS instance consumes the report queue and renders PDFs.
#
# ★ On the VPS this is no longer read from here: `docker-compose.prod.yml` sets
# it explicitly — `false` on every `api` replica and `true` on the single
# `reports-worker` container. It stays `true` in this example because a
# developer running one process wants both. docs/PDF_SPIKE.md §3.
REPORTS_WORKER_ENABLED=true

# How many API processes the VPS runs — Order А/261, criterion 6 (20,000
# concurrent users).
#
# ★ One Node process is one core whatever the machine has, which is the ceiling
# `docs/LOAD_TEST.md` measured. Raising this is the lever; it is safe only
# because rate limiting counts in Redis (`rate-limit.service.ts`) and PDF
# rendering has its own container. **Re-measure before claiming a number** —
# past some point Postgres connections, not cores, become the limit.
API_REPLICAS=2

# --- Auth --------------------------------------------------------------
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48
JWT_SECRET=replace-me-with-a-48-byte-random-value
REFRESH_SECRET=replace-me-with-a-different-48-byte-random-value
# Leave EMPTY — including in production. nomadkids.mn and api.nomadkids.mn
# share a registrable domain, so a host-only cookie is already sent on the web
# app's credentialed requests. Setting a Domain would only widen the cookie to
# every subdomain. docs/SECURITY.md §3.1.
COOKIE_DOMAIN=
ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL=15m
REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL=30d

# --- Object storage (S3-compatible: MinIO locally, R2 in production) ----
STORAGE_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9002
STORAGE_REGION=auto
STORAGE_BUCKET=kinder-media
STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
STORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
# Presigned URL lifetime in seconds. Short by design — docs/SECURITY.md §7.
STORAGE_PRESIGN_TTL=300

# --- Web ---------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# The object-storage origin, for the Content-Security-Policy only.
#
# `GET /v1/media/:id` redirects to a presigned URL on this host, and CSP is
# enforced against the URL the browser finally fetches — so without it every
# photo in the product is blocked by `img-src`. Same value as STORAGE_ENDPOINT
# locally; in production, the R2 S3 endpoint the presigned URLs are issued on.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MEDIA_URL=http://localhost:9002

# The site's own public origin, for `metadataBase` — it turns the OpenGraph
# image into the absolute URL a chat app or a search engine has to fetch.
#
# ★ Not the same setting as WEB_ORIGIN below, though they hold the same value.
# That one is read by the API when it builds a password-reset link; this one is
# inlined into the browser bundle at build time. A NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable and a
# server secret must not share a name.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Web app origin ---------------------------------------------------
# Used to build the password-reset link. One origin, not a list: a link has to
# name exactly one, and picking the first of CORS_ORIGINS would be a guess.
WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# --- Email (password reset only) --------------------------------------
# Optional as a SET. Leave all of it empty and the API still issues valid reset
# tokens — it simply cannot deliver them, and /health/readiness reports that
# honestly. Half-configured (host without from-address, or vice versa) is
# refused at boot in production, because it looks configured and fails only
# when a parent needs it.
#
# Port 465 = implicit TLS. Port 587 = STARTTLS. Getting this backwards produces
# a connection that hangs rather than an error.
# Fill all of these together, or none. Example MAIL_FROM:
#   MAIL_FROM=NomadKids <noreply@nomadkids.mn>
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
MAIL_FROM=

# --- ESIS (ministry education information system) ----------------------
# Optional as a SET, like SMTP above. Leave all of it empty and every existing
# feature works unchanged; only the ESIS boundary reports itself unconfigured.
# Half-configured is refused at boot in production, because it looks configured
# and then fails as an authentication error from the ministry rather than as
# our own missing setting.
#
# ★ ESIS_TOKEN is a credential. It is read only by the API, never sent to the
# browser, never logged, and deliberately NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_. The base
# URL must be https in production — the token crosses it on every request.
#
# API host, not the developer portal. Keep empty until the token and institution
# id are issued; production rejects a partially configured set.
# ESIS_BASE_URL=https://hubv2.esis.edu.mn
ESIS_BASE_URL=
ESIS_TOKEN=
ESIS_INSTITUTION_ID=
# Milliseconds. A ministry endpoint that stops answering must not hold our
# requests open until the platform proxy gives up.
ESIS_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# --- QPay (нэмэлт.md §8 — online payment) --------------------------------
# Optional as a SET, exactly like ESIS above. Leave all of it empty and every
# existing feature works unchanged — invoices, manual CASH/BANK_TRANSFER
# payments, the whole accountant module — and a parent's invoice simply shows
# no "QPay-ээр төлөх" button. Half-configured is refused at boot in
# production, same reasoning as SMTP/ESIS: it looks configured and then fails
# as a bank error instead of our own missing setting.
#
# Get these by registering as a QPay merchant (https://qpay.mn) — QPAY_USERNAME
# and QPAY_PASSWORD authenticate the merchant account, QPAY_INVOICE_CODE is
# assigned when the merchant is provisioned, not chosen locally. The sandbox
# base URL below is QPay's own; production merchants get a production URL at
# onboarding. See docs/reference/QPAY_INTEGRATION.md for the assumed API shape
# — it has not been exercised against a live sandbox, for lack of credentials.
#
# ★ No trailing /v2. `QpayClient` appends "/v2/auth/token", "/v2/invoice" and
# "/v2/payment/check" itself, so a base URL that already ends in /v2 produces
# /v2/v2/... and every call 404s.
QPAY_BASE_URL=https://merchant-sandbox.qpay.mn
QPAY_USERNAME=
QPAY_PASSWORD=
QPAY_INVOICE_CODE=
# Where QPay calls back after a payment. Must be a public HTTPS URL their
# servers can reach — localhost never works here, even in development; use a
# tunnel (e.g. ngrok) if you need to exercise the callback locally.
QPAY_CALLBACK_URL=
# Milliseconds, same reasoning as ESIS_TIMEOUT_MS.
QPAY_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# --- Portal access fee (client, 2026-09-01) ------------------------------
# One child, one school year, in tögrög. This is the ONLY thing QPay is used
# for: tuition and meal invoices are still raised and still settled, but by
# cash or bank transfer recorded by the accountant, never through the gateway.
#
# ★ "0" turns the gate OFF and is the default. A deployment that has not been
# given a price serves the portal exactly as it did before this existed —
# nobody is locked out of their own child's records by an unset variable.
ACCESS_FEE_AMOUNT=0
